  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tripartite constituents in The Bahamas have increased capacity to match skills with labour market needs</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth unemployment is a major challenge in The Bahamas. Shortcomings in education and training are among the key barriers to accessing the labour market identified in the 2020 UN Common Country Analysis (CCA). In 2024 and 2025, the ILO supports the Department of Labour to develop an apprenticeship programme at the national level for youth to acquire the skills demanded by the labour market.

The strategy of the intervention includes advice and training for policy formulation based on the principles of the Quality Apprenticeships Recommendation, 2023 (No. 208), and the implementation of a national apprenticeship programme.</narrative>
  </description>
